# cut — real-world examples

## Extract the third #-delimited field from input

```sh
cut -d'#' -f3
```

## Usernames from /etc/passwd (first :-delimited field)

```sh
cut -d: -f1 /etc/passwd
```

## Multiple fields at once

```sh
# user and shell from passwd
cut -d: -f1,7 /etc/passwd
```

## Fixed character ranges

```sh
# First 10 characters of every line
cut -c1-10 server.log
```

## Homelab: pull IPs out of an ssh auth log

```sh
grep 'Failed password' /var/log/auth.log | awk '{print $(NF-3)}' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn
# or with cut when the column position is fixed:
who | cut -d'(' -f2 | tr -d ')'
```

| Flag | What it does                       |
| ---- | ---------------------------------- |
| -d   | field delimiter (default TAB)      |
| -f   | select fields                      |
| -c   | select character positions         |
| -b   | select byte positions              |
| --complement | invert the selection        |
